+# Export acceptance and restart recovery hunt
+
+Checked revision: `a3869d3a31905ebc6d4691a25eab8ea4d05aa57d`.
+Scope: `Queue.submit`, `Queue.work`, `Queue.recover`, and `Queue.result` in
+`app/export_queue.py`, against `app/export-contract.md`. Stopped after this
+operation and its recovery path. Product code, governing records, and existing
+evidence are unchanged.
+
+## Finding: accepted work is permanently stranded after interruption (high)
+
+The contract requires accepted jobs to eventually produce their result after
+recovery (`app/export-contract.md:8–18`). This applies to a single worker that
+restarts after its predecessor stops; no concurrency or storage loss is needed.
+
+`work` commits `state = 'running'` before output (`app/export_queue.py:33–36`).
+If the process stops at that boundary, the job and its payload remain durable,
+but there is no result. The next constructor invokes `recover`, which does
+nothing (`:15–19`). Every subsequent `work` selects only `pending` rows
+(`:28–32`), so the durable `running` job is never selected again. Repeating
+`submit` with the same ID and payload returns acceptance but `INSERT OR IGNORE`
+does not make the existing row eligible (`:21–25`).
+
+Reproduction: `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 tests/hunt_witness.py`.
+The witness uses a temporary SQLite file and a real child process. It accepts
+`job-1` with payload `payload`, then calls `os._exit(73)` from the supported
+post-commit hook. Only after that process exits does a fresh worker open the
+database. Five work calls, a repeated same-payload submission, and five more
+work calls leave `state=('running',)` and `result('job-1') is None`.
+
+Observed result: **exit 1**, three tests run, one failure:
+
+```text
+test_accepted_claimed_job_survives_process_interruption ... FAIL
+test_accepted_pending_job_survives_restart ... ok
+test_completed_job_needs_no_work_after_restart ... ok
+AssertionError: None != 'payload' : Accepted job lost after restart and repeated work: state=('running',)
+```
+
+The ten calls demonstrate the symptom, rather than defining an eventuality
+deadline. Permanent stranding follows from the state transitions: neither
+recovery nor repeated submission changes this row, and work excludes it.
+The witness exits zero when all its promised behaviors hold and nonzero on
+violation. It checks the result rather than requiring a particular recovery
+implementation. A repair needs to make durable unfinished work eligible again
+under the supported sequential restart model; no repair was applied.
+
+## Coverage and limits
+
+| Boundary or obligation | Check | Outcome |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Successful acceptance durably records pending work | Read submission transaction; close and reopen temporary database, then work | Pass for tested input |
+| Ordinary work produces the accepted payload | Executable pending-restart control | Pass |
+| Interruption after claim commit, before output | Real process exit at supported hook, fresh worker, repeated work and same-payload submission | Contract violation above |
+| Completed work survives restart and needs no further work | Executable completed-restart control, including repeated same-payload submission | Pass |
+| Output and done-state transaction | Read `work`: result insertion and done update share one SQLite transaction | A rollback before commit leaves the previously committed running state; same recovery defect. No separate I/O fault injection performed |
+| Process interruption before claim commit or after final commit | Read transaction boundaries; pending and completed restart controls cover corresponding durable states | No additional finding; not an exhaustive crash-point test |
+
+Records discovery covered root `specs/`, the affected app paths, and references
+to queue/recovery identifiers and discovered record IDs. No narrower app/tests
+records or external queue consumers were found. The root local-only gate was
+respected: all execution and temporary data stayed local. The note payload,
+import metadata, and `data/` single-writer records describe other surfaces;
+this hunt did not verify their claims or read historical proof/verification
+reports. The queue's supported recovery obligation is supplied by the requested
+export contract.
+
+Not tested: simultaneous workers, overlapping requests, changing an ID's
+payload, storage loss, or database corruption, all outside the supported
+contract. No unrelated note/config/import investigation, claim verification,
+or governing-record maintenance was performed.
